#: ../../using/editors.rst:7
msgid "Editors and IDEs"
msgstr "Editoren und IDEs"

#: ../../using/editors.rst:9
msgid ""
"There are a number of IDEs that support Python programming language. Many "
"editors and IDEs provide syntax highlighting, debugging tools, and :pep:`8` "
"checks."
msgstr ""
"Es gibt eine Reihe von IDEs, die die Programmiersprache Python unterstützen. "
"Viele Editoren und IDEs bieten Syntaxhervorhebung, Debugging-Werkzeuge "
"und :pep:`8`-Prüfungen."

#: ../../using/editors.rst:14
msgid "IDLE --- Python editor and shell"
msgstr "IDLE --- Python Editor und Shell"

#: ../../using/editors.rst:16
msgid ""
"IDLE is Python’s Integrated Development and Learning Environment and is "
"generally bundled with Python installs. If you are on Linux and do not have "
"IDLE installed see :ref:`Installing IDLE on Linux "
"<installing_idle_on_linux>`. For more information see the :ref:`IDLE docs "
"<idle>`."
msgstr ""
"IDLE ist Pythons integrierte Entwicklungs- und Lernumgebung und wird in der "
"Regel zusammen mit Python-Installationen ausgeliefert. Wenn du Linux "
"verwendest und IDLE nicht installiert ist, siehe :ref:`Installieren von IDLE "
"unter Linux <installing_idle_on_linux>`. Weitere Informationen findest du in "
"der :ref:`IDLE-Dokumentation <idle>`."

#: ../../using/editors.rst:22
msgid "Other Editors and IDEs"
msgstr "Andere Editoren und IDEs"

#: ../../using/editors.rst:24
msgid ""
"Python's community wiki has information submitted by the community on "
"Editors and IDEs. Please go to `Python Editors <https://wiki.python.org/moin/"
"PythonEditors>`_ and `Integrated Development Environments <https://"
"wiki.python.org/moin/IntegratedDevelopmentEnvironments>`_ for a "
"comprehensive list."
msgstr ""
"Pythons Community-Wiki enthält von der Community eingereichte Informationen "
"zu Editoren und IDEs. Eine umfassende Liste findest du unter `Python Editors "
"<https://wiki.python.org/moin/PythonEditors>`_ und `Integrated Development "
"Environments <https://wiki.python.org/moin/"
"IntegratedDevelopmentEnvironments>`_."
